{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "customer-auth-collection",
    "name": "Customer Auth",
    "description": "# Customer Auth Postman Collection\n\nThis collection covers all customer authentication endpoints after the OTP-only redesign.\n\n## Auth Model\n- **Sign-up**: phone number + OTP only (the only path to creating an account).\n- **Sign-in**: phone + OTP *or* email + OTP (email OTP requires the email to already be attached to an existing account — no auto-registration).\n- **Passwords**: completely removed. `/sign-up/email` and `/sign-in/email` both return 400.\n\n## How to use this collection\n1. Select the **Customer Auth (Local)** environment.\n2. Run folders **top-to-bottom in order** — session cookies are managed automatically by Postman's cookie jar.\n3. **OTP codes** only appear in the **server console log** (`[CUSTOMER AUTH OTP]` / `[CUSTOMER AUTH EMAIL OTP]`). After hitting any Send OTP request, copy the code from the console, paste it into the `otpCode` environment variable, then run the matching Verify request.\n4. Re-running Sign-Up with the same phone number is expected to sign in (not create a duplicate).\n\n## Folders\n1. Sign-Up (Phone OTP) — create a brand-new account\n2. Sign-In (Phone OTP) — sign in with an existing phone number\n3. Sign-In (Email OTP) — sign in with an email already linked to an account\n4. Session & Sign-Out — verify session, then end it\n5. Negative / Regression Tests — confirm disabled flows fail correctly\n6. Cart — requires an active session\n7. Wishlist — requires an active session",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Sign-Up (Phone OTP)",
      "description": "Creates a brand-new customer account via phone number + OTP. This is the **only** path to account creation — there is no email/password sign-up.\n\n**Run order:** Send OTP → copy code from server console → paste into `otpCode` env var → Verify OTP.",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const origin = pm.environment.get('customerOrigin') || 'http://localhost:3000';",
              "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Origin', value: origin });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Send Phone OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response confirms code sent', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('message');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{customerPhone}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/phone-number/send-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "customers", "auth", "phone-number", "send-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Sends an OTP to the given phone number.\n\n**After running:** Look for `[CUSTOMER AUTH OTP] Phone: ... | Code: XXXXXX` in the **server console**. Copy the 6-digit code into the `otpCode` environment variable, then run **Verify OTP (creates account)**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Verify OTP (creates account)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains user with phoneNumber', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('user');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.user).to.have.property('phoneNumber');",
                  "    const userId = jsonData.user.id || jsonData.user._id;",
                  "    pm.expect(userId).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.environment.set('lastUserId', userId);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Phone number is verified', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const verified = jsonData.user?.phoneNumberVerified === true || jsonData.phoneNumberVerified === true;",
                  "    pm.expect(verified, 'phoneNumberVerified should be true after OTP verification').to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{customerPhone}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{otpCode}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/phone-number/verify",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "customers", "auth", "phone-number", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies the phone OTP. On first call for a new number this **creates the account**. On subsequent calls it signs in to the existing account.\n\n**Prerequisite:** Copy the OTP from the server console after running Send Phone OTP and paste it into the `otpCode` env var."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
