    {
      "name": "Negative / Regression Tests",
      "description": "Confirms that disabled, removed, or constrained flows return the expected rejection rather than behaving as they previously did.\n\nNone of these requests should succeed (200). All are expected to return a 4xx.",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const origin = pm.environment.get('customerOrigin') || 'http://localhost:3000';",
              "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Origin', value: origin });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "REG-1: Email OTP sign-in — unregistered email (must reject, not create)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Step 1 of 2 — send the OTP to a ghost email.",
                  "// The send step always returns 200 (prevents email enumeration).",
                  "// The actual rejection happens in REG-2 when we try to verify.",
                  "pm.test('Send OTP returns 200 (send step does not reveal existence)', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"ghost-unregistered@example.com\",\n  \"type\": \"sign-in\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/email-otp/send-verification-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "customers", "auth", "email-otp", "send-verification-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Sends a sign-in OTP for an email that has **no matching user** in the database.\n\nExpected: **200** — the send step deliberately does not reveal whether the email is registered (email-enumeration protection).\n\n**Confirmed behavior (`disableSignUp: true`):** When the email has no matching user, better-auth returns 200 but **silently discards the OTP** — it never calls `sendVerificationOTP` and never writes a verification record. Nothing will appear in the server console log. This is by design.\n\nProceed directly to REG-2 — no code to paste, any dummy code will be rejected."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "REG-2: Email OTP sign-in — verify with unregistered email (must 4xx, no account created)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 4xx — unregistered email rejected at sign-in verify step', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(400, 499);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response body is captured for review', function () {",
                  "    // Log the full response so you can inspect what error better-auth returns.",
                  "    console.log('REG-2 response body:', JSON.stringify(pm.response.json(), null, 2));",
                  "    pm.expect(true).to.be.true; // always passes — manual review of console log",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"ghost-unregistered@example.com\",\n  \"otp\": \"000000\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/sign-in/email-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "customers", "auth", "sign-in", "email-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Attempts to complete the email OTP sign-in for an address with no existing user.\n\nExpected: **4xx** — because `disableSignUp: true` caused the send step to silently discard the OTP (no record was stored), any code submitted here will be rejected as not found / invalid.\n\nThe OTP body is hardcoded to `000000` — there is no valid code to paste because none was ever issued.\n\n**After running:** Check the Postman console for the logged response body (the test script logs it automatically). Also confirm in MongoDB Compass that `customerUser` has **zero** documents with `email: ghost-unregistered@example.com`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "REG-3: POST /sign-up/email — must return 400 (not enabled)",
